<BaseLayout title="Nikita Mondal – Author" description="Nikita Mondal writes the calculation guides for Percentage Increase Calculator.">
  <header class="page-head wrap"><h1>Nikita Mondal</h1><p>Author of the practical guides on Percentage Increase Calculator.</p></header>
  <section class="content-page"><div class="content-grid wrap"><article class="prose">
    <h2>About the author</h2>
    <p>Nikita Mondal writes and organizes the site’s explanations of percentage increases, reverse percentages, spreadsheet formulas, and common calculation mistakes.</p>
    <p>The articles use direct formulas and worked examples. They are general educational material, not financial, tax, legal, employment, or investment advice.</p>
    <h2>Editorial approach</h2>
    <p>Each guide answers one specific question. Examples are recalculated from the stated formula, and terms such as percent, percentage points, and multiplier are defined when they first matter.</p>
    <h2>How the guides are checked</h2>
    <p>Before a guide is published, its worked examples are compared with the calculator rules. Edge cases such as a zero starting value, a decrease, decimal inputs, and repeated increases are explained separately rather than hidden behind one result.</p>
    <p>The <a href="/methodology/">calculation methodology</a> documents the formulas, rounding, accepted inputs, and test coverage used across the site.</p>
    <a class="tool-link" href="/guides/">Browse the percentage guides</a>
  </article><aside class="side-index"><strong>Explore</strong><a href="/#calculator">Calculator</a><a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a><a href="/about/">About</a></aside></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
